  "response_text": "If we don\u2019t set the Process Stack Pointer (PSP) before running the thread, the CPU doesn\u2019t know where the thread\u2019s stack is located. This leads to invalid memory accesses when the system tries to restore register values or execute from an undefined address, resulting in a hard fault. By using __set_PSP(stackptr), we ensure that the thread uses its correctly initialized stack, allowing the CPU to load the context safely and start the thread function.\\n",
